<title>SPAIN: Spain employers reject pressure to get labour deal.</title>
<headline>Spain employers reject pressure to get labour deal.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The president of Spanish employers' association CEOE Jose Maria Cuevas rejected on Tuesday any type of pressure to reach an accord with trade unions on labour reforms.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not going to sign just anything...We will assume all the costs that might go along with a disagreement, but we are convinced the deal must be effective,&quot; Cuevas told journalists.</p>
<p>The Popular Party government has said it would step in if the employers and unions failed to reach a sufficiently radical deal.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
